  "chapter": 320,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 30 Chapter 320\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8046, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the correction law, in relation to permitting the\n        correctional association to access, visit, inspect, and  examine\n        all state correctional facilities\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation  aims to provide the Correctional Association of New\nYork (CANY) with  authorization  to  oversee  conditions  in  all  state\ncorrectional  facilities  under  the  jurisdiction  of the Department of\nCorrections and Community Supervision (DOCCS or Department). The bill as\nwritten provides equivalent standing to  statutory  oversight  entities.\nSpecifically, it allows CANY access to any facility, at any time without\nnotice  to the Department, allows nearly unfettered access to all paper,\nelectronic, and video files in DOCCS  custody,  and  provides  immediate\nrecourse in court.\n \n  While  I  support  and  share the overall goals of this legislation, I\ncannot sign this bill into law in its current form. This legislation, as\nwritten, fails to  consider  the  logistical  realities  that  DOCCS  is\nresponsible for overseeing approximately 34,000 incarcerated individuals\ndaily-this  includes  providing  meals, recreation time, programming and\nother services to all incarcerated individuals, responding to  emergency\nand  non-emergency  incidents,  as well as generally ensuring the safety\nand security of incarcerated  individuals,  staff  and  the  facilities.\nFurther,  allowing  CANY  unlimited  access to any documentation, in any\nformat, also poses logistical and legal concerns.  Many documents  main-\ntained  by  the  Department  are protected from disclosure without prior\nauthorization under various statutes, such as Public Health Law,  Public\nOfficers  Law,  Mental Hygiene Law, and HIPPA, and places CANY a nonpro-\nfit, non-state entity in a place of preference over any other entity who\nmay have reason to visit or request or review documents.\n \n  In order to provide CANY with access to our state correctional facili-\nties while continuing to ensure DOCCS  has  the  right  to  protect  its\nfacilities,  I  have  secured  an agreement with the Legislature to make\ncertain changes to the bill. These changes include: CANY  providing  the\nDepartment 72 hours-notice prior to visiting the facility, CANY visitors\nwill  go through a vigorous background check before being permitted into\na facility, permitting DOCCS to restrict visits when the facility is  in\nlockdown  or  otherwise  experiencing an emergency. On the basis of this\nagreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
